<h2 id="fused">The three that vote</h2>
<ul class="cards">
<li class="card" id="m1b"><span class="role fused">fused · weight {{num:0.6|README.md#how-it-decides}}</span><h3>M1b: frozen XLS-R with a logistic probe</h3><p><strong>Technique:</strong> deep-learning anti-spoofing. <strong>What it measures:</strong> the hidden state of layer 7 of {{term:XLS-R}} (frozen), averaged over time, then a class-balanced logistic regression and a {{term:Platt map}}. M1b adds 40 VCTK real speakers from {{term:ASVspoof 2019}} and a spoof anchor to the training folds only. Layer 7 won inner cross-validation; mid-depth layers carry the acoustic detail that separates vocoders, the top layers are tuned for phonetic content.</p>
<p><strong>Numbers:</strong> inner {{num:0.301|README.md#numbers}}, holdout {{num:0.072|README.md#numbers}} (EER {{num:1.4%|README.md#numbers}}), In-the-Wild {{num:0.342|README.md#numbers}} (the results table rounds it {{num:0.343|README.md#results-at-a-glance}}), In-the-Wild false alarms {{num:0.8%|README.md#numbers}}, test share above {{num:0.5|README.md#numbers}} {{num:26.8%|README.md#numbers}}.</p>
<pre class="evidence-line">XLS-R layer-7 probe: calibrated log-likelihood ratio -5.78 (real-like, P=0.00)</pre>
<p class="src-note">{{src:README.md#how-it-decides|Sentence from the README's trace of HGT1046947.wav.}} Spec: <a href="specs/xlsr-probe.html">the XLS-R probe</a>.</p></li>
<li class="card" id="handcrafted"><span class="role fused">fused · weight {{num:0.2|README.md#how-it-decides}}</span><h3>Handcrafted spectral and prosody features</h3><p><strong>Techniques:</strong> spectral analysis and prosody. <strong>What it measures:</strong> {{num:234|README.md#the-eight-forensic-techniques}} features: spectral contrast, flatness, flux, roll-off, MFCC, LFCC and CQCC statistics, group-delay and phase-coherence cues; YIN pitch spread and slope, jitter and shimmer, loudness modulation, pauses, breath frames; {{term:gradient-boosted trees}} evaluated in numpy. Pitch variability is the one prosody cue that carried signal. The shipped version (v5b) is trained with augmented twins and validated on clean rows only.</p>
<p><strong>Numbers:</strong> inner {{num:0.469|README.md#numbers}}, holdout {{num:0.137|README.md#numbers}} (EER {{num:3.1%|README.md#numbers}}), In-the-Wild false alarms {{num:0.40%|README.md#numbers}}, test share above {{num:0.5|README.md#numbers}} {{num:45.1%|README.md#numbers}}. On its own it is blind to web-sourced fakes; that is why it gets a fifth of the vote, not half.</p>
<pre class="evidence-line">spectral/prosody features real-like (P=0.16): LFCC 16 frame-to-frame change 3.0 SD below real speech (toward synthetic); spectral contrast, band 0 0.8 SD above real speech (toward real); LFCC 1 variability 1.1 SD below real speech (toward real)</pre>
<p class="src-note">{{src:docs/reports/2026-09-26_worked-examples.md#4-hgt1046947wav-the-deep-detectors-disagree-drift-flagged-p--0003-z-mean-0686|Sentence from worked example 4.}} Spec: <a href="specs/handcrafted.html">handcrafted features</a>.</p></li>
<li class="card" id="m5"><span class="role fused">fused · weight {{num:0.2|README.md#how-it-decides}}</span><h3>M5: a trained head on XLS-R</h3><p><strong>Technique:</strong> deep-learning anti-spoofing. <strong>What it measures:</strong> the first 12 layers of XLS-R with learned layer weights, attentive statistics pooling and a linear head, trained on rented A100s with class-blind augmentation (noise, telephony band-limits, reverb, codecs, RawBoost). It did not clear its gate as a replacement for the probe, but it is wrong on different files, and as a third rank input it passed the second pre-declared sweep.</p>
<p><strong>Numbers:</strong> inner {{num:0.302|README.md#numbers}}, holdout {{num:0.363|README.md#numbers}} (EER {{num:6.0%|README.md#numbers}}), In-the-Wild false alarms {{num:0.45%|README.md#numbers}}, test share above {{num:0.5|README.md#numbers}} {{num:25.8%|README.md#numbers}}.</p>
<pre class="evidence-line">XLS-R fine-tuned head (M5, 12 layers, attentive pooling): logit +5.64 (synthetic-like, P=1.00)</pre>
<p class="src-note">{{src:README.md#how-it-decides|Sentence from the README's trace.}} Spec: <a href="specs/m5-head.html">the M5 head</a>.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="suppressor">The one that may only lower a score</h2>
<ul class="cards">
<li class="card" id="spectra"><span class="role">suppressor · weight 0</span><h3>Spectra-AASIST (M3)</h3><p><strong>Techniques:</strong> deep-learning anti-spoofing, spectral. <strong>What it measures:</strong> an off-the-shelf anti-spoofing model (its own XLS-R plus a graph-attention back end), run with no training through the same band-matched input path and crops; short clips are zero-padded to one window. Output: a spoof-minus-bonafide margin. <strong>Role:</strong> if the margin is below −3 and the fused rank is above {{num:0.5|scripts/fuse_sweep.py#L172}}, the rank is halved. It can never raise a score.</p>
<p><strong>Numbers, all possibly in-sample</strong> because its model card names no training set: inner {{num:0.0045|README.md#numbers}}, holdout {{num:0.012|README.md#numbers}} (EER {{num:0.16%|README.md#numbers}}), In-the-Wild {{num:0.065|README.md#numbers}} (its authors evaluated on that set), In-the-Wild false alarms {{num:0.0%|README.md#numbers}}, test share above {{num:0.5|README.md#numbers}} {{num:29.3%|README.md#numbers}}. The leakage probes support the suppressor role: the most perturbation-stable detector, the lowest miss rate on unseen generators, and a step that never raised the fused cost.</p>
<pre class="evidence-line">Spectra-AASIST: spoof-minus-bonafide margin +9.50 (synthetic-like, P=1.00)</pre>
<p class="src-note">{{src:README.md#how-it-decides|Sentence from the README's trace.}} Spec: <a href="specs/spectra-aasist.html">Spectra-AASIST</a>.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="evidence">Evidence and routing, never scored</h2>
<ul class="cards">
<li class="card" id="compression"><span class="role evidence">evidence</span><h3>Compression forensics</h3><p><strong>Technique:</strong> compression forensics. <strong>What it measures:</strong> {{num:19|README.md#the-eight-forensic-techniques}} codec-trace features in 3–7 kHz (spectral holes, floor depth, effective bandwidth), trained with both classes laundered through MP3/AAC so it cannot learn "MP3 = fake". It detects codec history well and the class barely, because the test set reads as laundered throughout. Its effective-bandwidth reading is a routing fact.</p>
<p><strong>Numbers:</strong> inner {{num:0.931|README.md#numbers}}, holdout {{num:0.900|README.md#numbers}} (EER {{num:20.1%|README.md#numbers}}), test share above {{num:0.5|README.md#numbers}} {{num:80.7%|README.md#numbers}}.</p>
<pre class="evidence-line">compression-trace features synthetic-like (P=0.97): whole-clip floor depth 1.7 SD below real speech (toward synthetic); 3-7 kHz valley depth 0.7 SD below real speech (toward synthetic); deep-hole flicker frame to frame 1.7 SD above real speech (toward synthetic)</pre>
<p class="src-note">{{src:docs/reports/2026-09-26_worked-examples.md#1-hgt1013455wav-confident-real-p--0002|Sentence from worked example 1, a confident real file.}} Spec: <a href="specs/compression.html">compression forensics</a>.</p></li>
<li class="card" id="container"><span class="role">routing</span><h3>Container and metadata</h3><p><strong>Technique:</strong> container, file forensics and metadata. <strong>What it measures:</strong> header facts (codec, rate, bit depth, encoder tag). Rule-based on purpose: on our training data the container <em>is</em> the label, and every test file carries the same FFmpeg tag, so it returns a constant score and routes compression forensics. It never reads filenames or filesystem timestamps, because git, zip and Docker rewrite them.</p>
<p><strong>Numbers:</strong> none by design (a constant {{num:0.5|README.md#what-did-not-work}} on this test set).</p>
<pre class="evidence-line">wav/pcm_s16le 16000 Hz mono 16-bit, 1 tag(s) [encoder=Lavf58.29.100]: no class evidence in the container; written by FFmpeg (libavformat), so the file was re-muxed or transcoded at least once</pre>
<p class="src-note">{{src:docs/reports/2026-09-26_worked-examples.md#worked-examples-eight-real-test-files-through-the-shipped-pipeline|The sentence every one of the eight files received.}} Spec: <a href="specs/container.html">container</a>.</p></li>
<li class="card" id="enf"><span class="role evidence">evidence</span><h3>ENF: mains hum</h3><p><strong>Technique:</strong> acoustic-environment consistency. <strong>What it measures:</strong> a 50 or 60 Hz hum and its stability on short windows. Rule-based and mild on purpose: stable hum is in a third of LJ Speech clips and almost no generated audio, so a learned version would learn "hum = real".</p>
<p><strong>Numbers:</strong> flags {{num:24|README.md#what-did-not-work}} test files; never moves a score.</p>
<pre class="evidence-line">no mains hum at 50 or 60 Hz (best 60 Hz candidate: median SNR 2.8 dB, above 12 dB in 0% of frames): no environment evidence either way</pre>
<pre class="evidence-line">enf: mains hum present, stable (recording-environment evidence)</pre>
<p class="src-note">{{src:docs/reports/2026-09-26_worked-examples.md#1-hgt1013455wav-confident-real-p--0002|First sentence from worked example 1;}} {{src:docs/reports/2026-09-26_worked-examples.md#5-hgt3237868wav-a-fake-with-a-stable-mains-hum-p--0935|the routing-log line from example 5, a fake with a stable hum.}} Spec: <a href="specs/enf.html">ENF</a>.</p></li>
<li class="card" id="splice"><span class="role evidence">evidence</span><h3>Splice and discontinuities</h3><p><strong>Technique:</strong> splice / discontinuity detection. <strong>What it measures:</strong> sample-level clicks and DC-offset jumps between {{num:100 ms|README.md#the-eight-forensic-techniques}} windows. On this data it finds vocoder artifacts more than edits, and the sponsor said no test clip is partially synthetic, so it is evidence.</p>
<p><strong>Numbers:</strong> flags {{num:58|README.md#what-did-not-work}} test files; never moves a score.</p>
<pre class="evidence-line">editing seam at 1.59 s: 1 click(s) (largest step 17x the surrounding waveform); consistent with a cut or inserted segment (background-floor range 26 dB, informational)</pre>
<p class="src-note">{{src:docs/reports/2026-09-26_worked-examples.md#8-hgt2305393wav-genuinely-uncertain-and-it-says-so-p--0471-z-mean-0995|Sentence from worked example 8.}} Spec: <a href="specs/splice.html">splice</a>.</p></li>
<li class="card" id="drift"><span class="role evidence">evidence</span><h3>Speaker drift</h3><p><strong>Technique:</strong> speaker-embedding consistency. <strong>What it measures:</strong> {{term:ECAPA}} embeddings on one-second windows; flags a voice that changes within the clip. The finding that keeps it out of the score: fakes are the <em>most</em> self-consistent voices, so fused it would push hard real recordings toward synthetic.</p>
<p><strong>Numbers:</strong> the mean window-to-window similarity separates classes toward fake at AUC {{num:0.73|README.md#what-did-not-work}}; drift flags {{num:16%|README.md#what-did-not-work}} of test files.</p>
<pre class="evidence-line">voice drifts across the clip: minimum window-to-window speaker similarity -0.10 over 14 windows</pre>
<p class="src-note">{{src:README.md#how-it-decides|Sentence from the README's trace.}} Spec: <a href="specs/speaker-drift.html">speaker drift</a>.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="gate-section">The gate</h2>
<ul class="cards">
<li class="card" id="gate"><span class="role">gate</span><h3>Speech gate</h3><p><strong>Part of the orchestration.</strong> <strong>What it measures:</strong> whether a file contains speech at all, from five cues: not silent, at least {{num:5%|README.md#the-eight-forensic-techniques}} voiced, pitch moving, loudness moving, not spectrally flat. Each threshold was set beyond the extreme value in the full test set, so it only catches silence, tones, static and noise; a file that fails skips fusion and goes to the {{term:pinned block}}.</p>
<p><strong>Numbers:</strong> gates {{num:0 of 1,671|README.md#the-eight-forensic-techniques}} test files.</p>
<pre class="evidence-line">speech present: voiced 28% of frames, pitch spread 0.34, loudness std 18.5 dB</pre>
<p class="src-note">{{src:README.md#how-it-decides|Sentence from the README's trace.}} Spec: <a href="specs/speech-gate-policy.html">the speech gate and the default-answer policy</a>.</p></li>
</ul>
